 "keyIdea": "Everyday things are made of materials such as wood, plastic, glass, metal, rock and fabric.",
 "explain": {
  "kid": [
   "Look around. A door is wood. A window is glass. A key is metal. A bag can be fabric or plastic.",
   "Each of these is a material."
  ],
  "adult": [
   "The core list for young children is wood, plastic, glass, metal, water, rock, brick, paper, card and fabric. Naming them gives words for later work on properties.",
   "Point out that one object can use several materials: a pencil is wood with graphite inside and a metal end."
  ]
 },
